WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:04.880
Some shrimp are unusually scrappy fighters.

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:07.560
Pistol shrimp and a few dozen others

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:12.260
can snap their claws shut at ultrafast speeds.

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:15.040
The claws close so fast that it boils

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:18.880
the water around them, creating tiny air bubbles.

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:21.420
The force of the water pressure crushing the bubbles

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:25.839
generates a shockwave that stuns the shrimp’s prey.

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:28.400
How claws that evolved for simple pinching

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:31.100
gained the ability to close so quickly

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:34.220
was a mystery to biologists.

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:36.560
A team of researchers looked closely at

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:40.700
the claw anatomies of 114 shrimp species.

00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:42.640
They found two types of claw joints

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:45.100
that no one had noticed before.

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:47.300
The first was a basic slip joint,

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:49.940
like you’d find in a Swiss Army Knife.

00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:53.100
A tiny ridge creates pressure as the claw
closes,

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:56.260
allowing it to snap shut a little more quickly.

00:00:56.260 --> 00:00:59.280
That basic slip joint set the evolutionary stage

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:02.980
for a further modification: the cocking slip joint.

00:01:02.980 --> 00:01:06.340
With this joint, the ridge cocks the claw fully open,

00:01:06.340 --> 00:01:08.840
building up tremendous muscle tension

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:11.800
before the shrimp releases it.

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:15.540
The scientists 3D-printed models of the various joints

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:19.280
and found that a claw with a cocking slip joint can snap

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:23.040
closed with enough force to generate shockwaves.

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:24.540
So maybe now you’ll think twice

00:01:24.540 --> 00:01:26.680
the next time you go toe-to-toe

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:29.440
or claw-to-claw with a pint-sized pistol shrimp!

